  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant for the Cambodia-Thailand Border Areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Thailand-Cambodia border crisis, triggered by renewed territorial conflict and political tensions, has led to widespread displacement, border closures, and humanitarian needs affecting over 300,000 people. With hundreds of thousands of Cambodian migrants in Thailand-many in vulnerable or irregular status-there is an urgent need for protection, basic services, and legal support. The Royal Thai Government has initiated a multi-sectoral response, but capacity is strained due to concurrent crises. In response, IOM proposes a coordinated, multi-sectoral humanitarian intervention to safeguard the rights and well-being of displaced populations, migrants, and returnees. This includes delivering life-saving assistance, protection services, and mental health support, while addressing misinformation and discrimination to promote safety and dignity for affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
